# Secrets & Environment
.env
# .env.db (the narrow db env projected for postgres/redis, T-32) and any
# future .env.<suffix> in this directory. NOT a leak being closed: the
# root .gitignore already carries `.env.*`, and a gitignore pattern
# without a slash matches at EVERY depth, so backend/.env.db is covered
# there today (verified with `git check-ignore -v`). This line is here
# for local explicitness -- the rule sits next to the files it protects,
# and it survives someone rewriting the root file.
../tmp/GT-41-fix-env-example/backend/.env.example
# Same exception as the root .gitignore, repeated here for the same reason the
# line above is: the rule should sit next to the files it protects. NOTE for
# anyone verifying this with `git check-ignore -v backend/.env.example`: that
# command answers "not ignored" for a TRACKED file whatever the patterns say.
# Use --no-index to see the rule that actually matches.
!.env.example

